  "established_findings": [
    "The two affected ranks booted with no connected display, no simpledrm framebuffer, and an NVIDIA NULL MetaMode.",
    "GNOME Shell never registered its GDM session on either affected rank, so GDM did not complete its declared responsibility to quit Plymouth.",
    "The unaffected rank had a connected display and simpledrm framebuffer, registered its GDM session, and completed Plymouth wait automatically in 3.314 seconds on the current boot and 5.764 seconds on the previous boot.",
    "Packages, semantic kernel options, GRUB and GDM configuration, on-disk unit fragments, and relevant drop-in state do not explain the rank split.",
    "Starting the standard Plymouth quit service completed systemd targets on the affected owner by conflicting with and stopping GDM; it did not restore a graphical session."
  ],
  "hypothesis": {
    "statement": "Absence of a boot display/framebuffer prevents the GDM greeter from registering, leaving Plymouth running indefinitely because this distribution delegates the quit operation to GDM.",
